The kubebuilder helm/v1-alpha plugin scaffolds templates/manager/manager.yaml
from the standard layout and then never updates it again (it is in the
plugin's "preserved unless --force" tier). Rather than commit the whole
generated file just to carry two edits, `make helm-chart` deletes it, lets the
plugin write a pristine copy, and applies this patch on top.

The two edits:
  - --enable-controller: .Values.global.controller selects which controller the
    manager runs, mirroring the same value gating which CRDs the crds subchart
    installs. Omitted when "all" so the manager keeps its default.
  - image tag: falls back to .Chart.AppVersion when .Values...image.tag is
    empty, which is what the Makefile stamps for the floating "latest" default.

If a kubebuilder bump changes the scaffold, `git apply` fails loudly. Refresh
this patch by editing the generated file and re-diffing it against a pristine
scaffold.

diff --git a/dist/chart/templates/manager/manager.yaml b/dist/chart/templates/manager/manager.yaml
--- a/dist/chart/templates/manager/manager.yaml
+++ b/dist/chart/templates/manager/manager.yaml
@@ -31,9 +31,13 @@ spec:
             {{- range .Values.controllerManager.container.args }}
             - {{ . }}
             {{- end }}
+            {{- $controller := (.Values.global | default dict).controller | default "all" }}
+            {{- if ne $controller "all" }}
+            - "--enable-controller={{ $controller }}"
+            {{- end }}
           command:
             - /manager
-          image: {{ .Values.controllerManager.container.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.controllerManager.container.image.tag }}
+          image: {{ .Values.controllerManager.container.image.repository }}:{{ .Values.controllerManager.container.image.tag | default .Chart.AppVersion }}
           {{- if .Values.controllerManager.container.env }}
           env:
             {{- range $key, $value := .Values.controllerManager.container.env }}
